rlpowell@digitalkingdom.org> wrote:

> On Fri, Nov 15, 2013 at 02:15:56PM -0800, Robin Lee Powell wrote:
> > On Thu, Nov 14, 2013 at 10:31:52PM -0800, Robin Lee Powell wrote:
> > >
> > > I asked you all for money to make lojban.org faster, and you
> > > responded (more than I expected, thank you!), apparently on the
> > > basis of me asserting that there was a problem.
> > >
> > > I forgot something important, though, which was to ask *you* if
> > > you think there's a problem.  I'm worried that I'm spending
> > > money to solve a problem only I can see (because it's my
> > > professional field).
> > >
> > > There are probably things I can do to make the server go faster,
> > > if I worked hard at it, but let's say, for expediency's sake,
> > > that the best I could do is to make it 25% faster than it is
> > > now.
> > >
> > > Given that, what do you think?  Is lojban.org slow enough that I
> > > should take people's money to make it better?
> >
> > I want to be really clear that I'm asking you to check *current*
> > performance.  We've made a number of changes recently.
> >
> > In fact, I *just* made a bunch of changes.  So, please, go try
> > things out (in particular the main wiki, jbovlaste, and vlasisku)
> > and tell me if you still think it's worth spending money.  Come
> > back in a day or so and let me know.
>
> OK, well, no-one is all like "OMG IT'S TOTALLY THE FASTEST THING
> NOW!!", so I will say *THANK YOU VERY MUCH*!, take your money, and
> make a new server.
>

What? I can only say that everything works now. I haven't noticed any
shutdowns for the last several days. So it's all fine. Thank you for the
upgrade, Robin!

[the fastest website for me is google.com]


